        "parms": "# dict — a named dictionary\nA dict holds entries: a key and a value. A value is any message, so chord holds the three numbers 0 4 7. Keys nest with ::, so voice::1::freq is one key three levels deep. Every dict with the same name in a patch shares one dictionary, and its contents are saved with the patch: synth starts with freq 440, gain 0.5 and chord 0 4 7.\nUnlike Max, there is no dump message: walk the entries with dict.iter or print them with dict.print. On this engine a message box keeps only its first word, so each command here is built with prepend. A loaded dictionary has its keys in alphabetical order, not the order they were written (yse-soundengine#1243).",
        "type": ".text"
      },
